# What the studio draws. Pictures of the app are worth looking at and not worth
# keeping: they are regenerated by `tools/shoot.sh` from whatever the working
# tree currently says, so a committed one is only ever out of date.
#
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. `shots/` unanchored also matched
# `docs/shots/`, which is the one set that IS committed — the README's pictures,
# regenerated by `.github/workflows/shots.yml` rather than by somebody
# remembering to, which is what makes them worth keeping.
/shots/

# Python bytecode from tools/. `contact.py` is imported directly when checking
# its own arithmetic, and CPython writes this beside it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
